# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Godot 4
# Import cache and generated resources. Rebuilt by `make import`.
.godot/
# Legacy Godot 3 import dir, harmless to keep listed
.import/
*.translation

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- builds
# `make release` output
build/
# Mono/C# artefacts. No C# in this project today, but the Mono editor build
# will drop these the moment anyone adds a script.
.mono/
bin/
obj/
*.csproj.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated evidence
# Screenshots and probe JSON from `tools/round.sh`. Roughly 8 MB per round and
# fully reproducible with `make round`, so there is no reason to version them.
#
# Exception: the six fixed-angle map shots of the default round. The README
# embeds them, so they have to be in the repo or the page renders broken
# images. `make shots` rewrites them in place, which is the point — the
# README always shows the current build.
shots/*
!shots/dev/
shots/dev/*
!shots/dev/map_*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- third-party reference
# reference/bar/ holds real Krunker.io gameplay screenshots (official Steam
# store captures and in-engine map renders from the wiki). They are somebody
# else's copyrighted material, gathered purely as a comparison target while
# building this, so they are deliberately NOT redistributed here.
# SOURCES.md lists every URL — re-fetch them locally if you want to run the
# visual critique. Delete these two lines if you have cleared the rights.
reference/bar/*
!reference/bar/SOURCES.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- os / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- notes
# export_presets.cfg IS committed on purpose: `make release` needs it and this
# one carries no signing identity, keystore path or password. If you add
# codesigning credentials, move them out or start ignoring this file.
